<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="DXC">
    <PackageVersion Include="Vortice.Dxc" Version="3.3.4" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Vortice.Direct3D12" Version="3.5.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="D3DCompiler (DXBC oracle backend — managed wrapper restores cross-platform; runtime is Windows-only, guarded by OperatingSystem.IsWindows())">
    <PackageVersion Include="Vortice.D3DCompiler" Version="3.3.4" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Vortice.Direct3D11" Version="3.3.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="SPIRV-Cross">
    <PackageVersion Include="Silk.NET.SPIRV.Cross.Native" Version="2.23.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    ImageSharp is deliberately capped at the 3.1.x line. 4.0.0 is not a technical upgrade
    problem, it is a LICENCE gate: its build targets hard-fail with "No Six Labors license
    found ... obtain a license from https://sixlabors.com/pricing/" unless a paid licence key
    or `sixlabors.lic` is present. 3.1.12 is the newest release that builds without one, and
    it is the current tip of 3.1.x. Same class of problem as the FluentAssertions relicensing
    that drove the Shouldly migration below - a licence gate, not a technical one.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Label="Rendering">
    <PackageVersion Include="Silk.NET.OpenGL"          Version="2.23.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Silk.NET.Windowing.Glfw"  Version="2.23.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="SixLabors.ImageSharp"     Version="3.1.12" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="MonoGame runtime validation (Phase 17 / Phase 18)">
    <PackageVersion Include="MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL" Version="3.8.2.1105" />
    <PackageVersion Include="MonoGame.Framework.WindowsDX" Version="3.8.2.1105" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Apos.Shapes is an EVIDENCE PIN, not a currency pin - do not bump it as part of a routine
    dependency sweep. Phase 55 uses the package's own embedded effect as the gallery baseline
    arm, which is only a valid comparison because the package's shader IS our vendored
    tests/fixtures/shaders/third-party/Apos.Shapes/apos-shapes-sm6.fx.

    0.7.7 pins upstream commit a85a31c, which matches that fixture modulo one comment line.
    Checked 2026-07-28: 0.7.12 pins a DIFFERENT commit (b69bd73) whose apos-shapes.fx differs by
    ~1150 lines and adds a FOURTH sampler - a new `ArcTex` at register t2 that pushes
    `BlueNoiseTex` to t3. Bumping therefore silently points the baseline arm at a different
    shader than the candidate. Moving this pin means vendoring the new upstream revision and
    re-running the whole Phase 55 proof; it is that phase's work, not a version bump.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Label="Apos.Shapes (Phase 55 - real ShapeBatch gallery render-proof)">
    <PackageVersion Include="Apos.Shapes" Version="0.7.7" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Test-only. None of these reach a consumer: the shipped src/ projects reference exactly
    Silk.NET.SPIRV.Cross.Native and Vortice.*, nothing here.

    ASSERTION LIBRARY: Shouldly, and FluentAssertions is BANNED (issue #171).

    FluentAssertions relicensed at 8.x to the Xceed "Community License Agreement (for
    Non-Commercial Use)", which requires a PAID commercial licence for any use by an
    organisation that earns revenue. We previously capped it at 7.2.2, the last Apache-2.0
    release - but a cap only defers the problem: the 7.x line receives no further fixes, so
    the choice was "migrate now" or "migrate later from a frozen, unmaintained dependency".
    We migrated. Shouldly is BSD-3-Clause at every version, with no commercial gate.

    Do not re-add FluentAssertions - not at 7.x, not "just for one test". Shouldly's entry
    points are ShouldBe/ShouldContain/... on the value itself, never .Should().
    See project_facts.md and project_decisions.md for the full rationale.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Label="Test">
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit"                        Version="2.9.3" />
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio"    Version="3.1.5" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk"       Version="18.8.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Shouldly"                     Version="4.3.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="coverlet.collector"           Version="10.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
